Now the tests. Add to the "enforces host, origin, fetch-site..." test:

```ts
// A cross-site click on the deployed URL still has to render the app shell.
const shellNavigation = await app.request("/", {
  headers: { "sec-fetch-site": "cross-site", "sec-fetch-mode": "navigate", "sec-fetch-dest": "document", accept: "text/html" },
});
assert.notEqual(shellNavigation.status, 403);

// Cross-site API requests and sub-resources stay blocked.
assert.equal((await app.request("/api/mode", {
  headers: { "sec-fetch-site": "cross-site", "sec-fetch-mode": "cors", "sec-fetch-dest": "empty" },
})).status, 403);
assert.equal((await app.request("/api/mode", {
  headers: { "sec-fetch-site": "cross-site", "sec-fetch-mode": "navigate", "sec-fetch-dest": "document" },
})).status, 403);
```

Wait: does `fixture` app have a "/" route? It's createApp only, no static. "/" → app.notFound → 404 JSON. That's fine: assert.notEqual 403.

But hold on: the app's `app.use("*")` matches "/"; host allowed localhost default; no basic auth. So 404.

Also add a positive same-site? `same-site` should be blocked for API. Fine.

Let me add the tests after line 123.

